entry.summary:
How to connect Two Database in innerjoin? CREATE EXTENSION dblink; Example: SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM Employee e JOIN dblink('dbname=department_db', 'SELECT dept_id, dept_name FROM Department') AS d(dept_id INT, dept_name TEXT) ON e.department_id = d.dept_id
;
Same Database: Example: SELECT e.name, d.dept_name
Now we Start , Tables Setup Employee table: emp_id | name | dept_id -------+--------+-------- 1 | Udaya | 2 2 | Mathavi | 3 3 | Kumar | 1 4 | Meena | NULL
Department table: dept_id | dept_name --------+----------- 1 | IT 2 | Finance 3 | HR 4 | Marketing
SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM Employee e INNER JOIN Department d ON e.dept_id = d.dept_id;
Output:
name dept_name
Udaya Finance
Mathavi HR
Kumar IT
!..Only employees with valid department. SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM Employee e LEFT JOIN Department d ON e.dept_id = d.dept_id;
Output: name | dept_name -------+----------- Udaya | Finance Priya | HR Kumar | IT Meena | NULL
!..All employees shown, even Meena (no department → NULL). SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM Employee e RIGHT JOIN Department d ON e.dept_id = d.dept_id;
Output: name | dept_name -------+----------- Udaya | Finance Priya | HR Kumar | IT NULL | Marketing
!..All departments shown, even Marketing (no employee → NULL). SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM Employee e FULL OUTER JOIN Department d ON e.dept_id = d.dept_id;
Output: name | dept_name -------+----------- Udaya | Finance Priya | HR Kumar | IT Meena | NULL NULL | Marketing
!..Combines LEFT + RIGHT → all employees + all departments. SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM Employee e CROSS JOIN Department d;
Output: name | dept_name -------+----------- Udaya | IT Udaya | Finance Udaya | HR Udaya | Marketing Priya | IT Priya | Finance ... (every combination)
!..Every employee paired with every department. Our next blog is Aggregate Function....
